  "verbalization": "Cyclophosphamide exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2b6 and Cyp2d6, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are known to catalyze the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, a process that generates bioactive lipid mediators. The observed pathway links Cyclophosphamide to Cyp2c18 through the intermediate of arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, suggesting that Cyclophosphamide may modulate Cyp2c18 function via a shared metabolic pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship, with the shared involvement of arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity as a critical mediator. The evidence supports the hypothesis that Cyclophosphamide influences Cyp2c18 through the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, potentially altering the metabolic profile of the enzyme. This mechanism is supported by the presence of a common intermediate in all three pathways, reinforcing the integrated role of arachidonic acid metabolism in linking Cyclophosphamide to Cyp2c18.",
